{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"Rscript script.R && sed -n '1,220p' spec-table.md && wc -w memo.md && file figures/spec-curve.png\"","aggregated_output":"Warning messages:\n1: Setting row names on a tibble is deprecated. \n2: Setting row names on a tibble is deprecated. \n3: Setting row names on a tibble is deprecated. \n4: Setting row names on a tibble is deprecated. \nWarning messages:\n1: No shared levels found between `names(values)` of the manual scale and the\ndata's colour values. \n2: No shared levels found between `names(values)` of the manual scale and the\ndata's colour values. \n3: No shared levels found between `names(values)` of the manual scale and the\ndata's colour values. \nBenchmark: 1794.342; naive observational contrast: -8497.516\n# NSW--CPS specification table\n\nExperimental benchmark (randomized NSW treated minus NSW control): **$1,794** (SE $671; 95% CI [$479, $3,109]).\n\n| Covariate set | Estimator | Common support | Treated N | CPS-control candidates N | Estimate (USD) | SE | 95% CI | Gap from benchmark |\n|---|---|:---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| None | Raw observational difference | No | 185 | 15992 | $-8,498 | $583 | [$-9,641, $-7,354] | $-10,292 |\n| Demographics | 1-NN matching | No | 185 | 15992 | $-2,798 | $1,139 | [$-5,030, $-566] | $-4,592 |\n| Demographics | Score stratification | No | 185 | 15992 | $-4,046 | $667 | [$-5,352, $-2,740] | $-5,840 |\n| Demographics | 1-NN matching | Yes | 185 | 12706 | $-2,972 | $1,016 | [$-4,962, $-982] | $-4,766 |\n| Demographics | Score stratification | Yes | 185 | 12706 | $-3,791 | $686 | [$-5,135, $-2,448] | $-5,586 |\n| Demographics + prior earnings | 1-NN matching | No | 185 | 15992 | $1,712 | $810 | [$125, $3,300] | $-82 |\n| Demographics + prior earnings | Score stratification | No | 185 | 15992 | $-181 | $644 | [$-1,444, $1,082] | $-1,975 |\n| Demographics + prior earnings | 1-NN matching | Yes | 185 | 5776 | $2,088 | $786 | [$547, $3,629] | $294 |\n| Demographics + prior earnings | Score stratification | Yes | 185 | 5776 | $1,249 | $645 | [$-16, $2,513] | $-545 |\n\nCommon support is the intersection of the fitted propensity-score ranges for NSW treated and CPS controls, estimated separately for each covariate set. All 185 treated observations were inside that intersection in both models; trimming therefore only removes CPS controls. The displayed CPS N is the candidate pool, not the number of distinct controls selected by matching.\n\nFor 1-NN rows, MatchIt forms ATT matches with replacement. Standard errors use an Abadie--Imbens-style analytic conditional-variance estimator with three same-arm nearest neighbours for local outcome variances and control reuse counts; no ordinary bootstrap is used. Stratification uses five score strata defined by treated-score quintiles and a fixed-strata sampling variance. These intervals do not propagate uncertainty from estimating the propensity-score model.\n     419 memo.md\nfigures/spec-curve.png: PNG image data, 3520 x 2080, 8-bit/color RGB, non-interlaced\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
